  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_variegatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Labeo cyclorhynchus becomes about 16 cm long. The name \"variegatus\" is regarded nowadays only as a synonym of Labeo cyclorhynchus. The checkered variety occurs in the wild but bears no scientific name of its own.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_variegatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species of Labeo is imported from the Congo.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_variegatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Like all Labeos these fish are quarrelsome against conspecifics, but L. cyclorhynchus in particular is regarded as quite peaceful against other species of fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_variegatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Usually this species has long, sickle-shaped dorsal fins. But one of the specimens has a \"normal\"-shaped dorsal fin. This possibly is a sexual dimorphism. Possibly the \"Variegatus\" morph is most often linked to male specimens? So far nobody knows.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/labeo_variegatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The checkered variety is maybe best compared with the so-called OB-morphs in Mbuna cichlids from Lake Malawi. The \"normal\" variety of Labeo cyclorhynchus is hardly ever imported.</p>"
    }
  ],
